## Products 

  

### Alchemer Iris (NEW — announced September 2, 2026)

**URL:** https://www.alchemer.com/iris 

**Tagline:** "See every signal. Focus where it matters." 

Alchemer Iris is Alchemer's AI-native, human-first platform for customer feedback and intelligence. It unifies signals from surveys, in-app feedback, reviews, social, and listings into one place, then uses AI to surface themes, sentiment, and risk, and to turn those insights into action — automating review responses, triggering follow-ups, and routing insights into the systems teams already use. 

Key capabilities: 

- **Conversational / prompt-first navigation** — users describe their objective in natural language and Iris guides them to the right capability or next step 

- **AI Survey Builder** — automatically generates surveys based on stated business objectives, built on Alchemer's survey design best practices 

- **AI Removal Assistant** — identifies potentially policy-violating reviews and assists with removal requests 

- **Action & workflow automation** — connects insights to operational actions across systems 

- **Human-in-the-loop controls** — configurable controls, audit trails, and guardrails; Alchemer emphasizes that users decide where and how AI is applied, rather than full automation 

Iris is built on purpose-built AI combining NLP, aspect-based sentiment analysis (ABSA) machine learning, and generative AI. Alchemer describes Iris as consolidating the AI capabilities it has introduced since 2024 — including Pulse, Pulse AI, Spark, AI Highlights, Predictive Analytics, Automated Survey Follow-Up, and AI Auto-Responder — into one unified, AI-native architecture, and as bringing together the Compass, Collect, Connect, and Clarity product lines. 

**Availability:** Not yet generally available as of this update. Iris is in a controlled rollout / waitlist phase — the live site's call-to-action is "Join the Waitlist" ("Be first in line when the beta opens. We'll follow up with onboarding details as soon as your spot is confirmed."). Beta/general availability is planned to begin Q4 2026 for select customers, with expansion planned across customer segments. A webinar, "A first look at Alchemer Iris," was scheduled for September 29, 2026. Check https://www.alchemer.com/iris for the current access status. 

**Executive quotes:** CEO Martin Mrugal: "The organizations that win won't be the ones with the most feedback or the best dashboards; they'll be the ones that shorten the distance between hearing something and doing something about it." CCO Ryan Tamminga: "While Iris can automate the feedback-to-action cycle, our goal is to extend human expertise and supplement where needed." 

